   "cluster": 0,
   "theme": "Agricultural Contaminant Loss via Tile Drainage",
   "description": "This umbrella theme spans the export of nutrients (nitrate, phosphorus), agrochemicals (herbicides, pesticides), and microbial contaminants (bacteria, manure-derived pathogens) from agricultural fields through subsurface tile drainage systems. It encompasses the soil structural and hydrological controls governing these losses, their quantification and modeling, and the influence of drainage and land management practices on contaminant concentrations and fluxes.",
